## Stop sidebar expand-then-collapse flash on page load

Context:
The sidebar defaults to collapsed, but CSS painted it expanded (200px) and
only applied `.collapsed` on DOMContentLoaded, so the width transition
animated expanded→collapsed on every new page. The collapse preference is
now applied before first paint, and width transitions are suppressed until
the restore has run.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/sidebar-collapse-init.js (new)
   Synchronous pre-paint script that sets `html.ob-sidebar-collapsed` from
   localStorage (default collapsed).
2. src/front/templates/base.html
   Loads the pre-paint script in `<head>` without defer.
3. src/front/static/global/css/sidebar-layout.css
   Collapsed geometry honours `html.ob-sidebar-collapsed`; transitions are
   disabled until `html.ob-sidebar-ready`.
4. src/front/static/global/js/sidebar-nav.js
   `_applyCollapsed` keeps the nav `.collapsed` class and the html class in
   sync; toggle and restore use it; marks the page ready after restore.
5. tests/units/front/test_sidebar_collapse_prepaint.py (new)
   Contract tests for the pre-paint script, CSS hooks, and toggle sync.
6. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   Documents the pre-paint collapse contract.

